<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kenya African National Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1960</span> · Also known as KANU</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kenya African National Union (KANU) is a Kenyan political party founded in 1960 and led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jomo-kenyatta">Jomo Kenyatta</a>, which took the country to independence in 1963. It ruled Kenya without interruption for almost four decades, becoming the sole legal party under Daniel arap Moi in 1982. It lost power when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwai-kibaki">Mwai Kibaki</a> won the election of 2002.</p></div>
